# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# trendza — environment variables (ALL OPTIONAL)
#
# The demo runs fully offline with ZERO configuration: `npm install && npm run
# dev` and it works — clothes come from a local seed, saved outfits live in the
# browser's localStorage. Nothing here is required.
#
# ── Web search (recommended for the full effect) ────────────────────────────
# The Clip → "Search web" flow hits the real `search-clothes` edge function and
# returns genuine Google Shopping products. To enable it locally, copy this
# file to `.env.local` and fill in your Supabase project's URL + publishable
# anon key. (The hosted Vercel demo sets these privately, so the live link
# already has live search without touching this file.)
VITE_DEMO_SEARCH_URL=
VITE_DEMO_SEARCH_ANON=

# ── Full real backend (AI try-on + style analysis) ─────────────────────────
# Setting these switches the app to the genuine Supabase client and brings the
# paid AI edge functions (Qwen try-on, style analysis) online. Note this also
# enables real auth, so reviewers face a sign-in wall instead of the frictionless
# demo gate.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────